  "body": "The iTNC 530 programming station rejects the peck drilling block that `heidenhain.cps` writes for the sample in #3095. The station runs NC software `606425 004 SP20`.\n\n1. Use `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/heidenhain/drill_peck.nc` at `c5f4e6f94`.\n2. Import the original file as `VMC_3-AXIS.I`.\n3. Read the program back from the station converter. The station prefixes the entire `N100 G205` block with `ERROR =`. Both converter commands return zero.\n\nA repeat import gave the same error. In a separate copy, we changed only `Q208=FMAX` to `Q208=+60`. The station then returned the complete cycle block, including `Q395=+0`. We used the numeric value only to isolate the parser error. The correct retract feed depends on the intended cycle behavior.\n\nDone means the post emits a supported value that preserves the requested retract behavior, or refuses the operation with a diagnostic. Add a regression test and check the output on the programming station. The physical Fehlmann uses NC software `340490-03`. Its test is pending.\n\nSuggested labels: `bug`, `area:post`, `source:agent`, `P1`, `effort:high`. The defect changes posted NC code.\n",
